{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1547882-sp-ultra-first-aid-vs-healing","id":1547882,"title":"SP Ultra: \"first aid\" vs. \"healing\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-21T14:48:41-08:00","id":1547882,"title":"SP Ultra: \"first aid\" vs. \"healing\"","content":"A lot of the combat status effects in SP Ultra resolve when &quot;The character benefits from first aid&quot;. But the term &quot;first aid&quot; is nowhere defined in the draft manuscript; the only place it appears outside of a status effect is in the explanation of the Medicine Skill, which says giving first aid is a Medicine + Cunning action. Meanwhile, the section on healing states that treating injuries is a Medicine + Intellect action.<br /> <br /> So ... is the healing action the same thing as &quot;first aid&quot;, or not? It would make logical sense if they were the same ... but they don't use the same Attribute. And if they're different, when can you give first aid, and how does it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}